    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Feats\" title=\"Feats\">Feats</a></i></p><p>You are skilled at fending off attacks of many forms.</p><p><b>Effect:</b> You gain a +1 bonus to your <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Reflex_Defense\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Reflex Defense\">Reflex Defense</a>, <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Fortitude_Defense\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Fortitude Defense\">Fortitude Defense</a>, and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Will_Defense\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Will Defense\">Will Defense</a>.</p><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Additional_Improved_Defenses_Effects\">Additional Improved Defenses Effects</span></h2><p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Starships_of_the_Galaxy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy</a></i></p><p><b>Special:</b> This Feat does not apply to the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle_Combat\" title=\"Vehicle Combat\">Defenses</a> of a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a>, even if you are piloting or commanding it. This is one reason many <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilots\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pilots\">Pilots</a> prefer the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Dodge\" title=\"Dodge\">Dodge</a> Feat to Improved Defenses.</p>",
